 "caveats": [
  "SURVIVOR BIAS: survivors-only backtest universe, so CAGR is an UPPER BOUND. Of ~721 S&P names that left the index 2011-2026, only ~40 are genuine bankruptcies (the rest are M&A / ticker-changes, NOT losses) and are excluded from the panel. The failure-bias is bounded (momentum/quality screens avoid most pre-bankruptcy names) but real - not a survivorship-free track record.",
  "Backtested 2011-2026, NOT a forward projection. Walk-forward tests show realized returns ~40% of backtest CAGR; per-2yr regime CAGR ranged 2% to 61% (median 33%).",
  "TRUE daily mark-to-market - the -43% drawdown is the real intra-period low (COVID 2020), not a smoothed rebalance-spaced figure.",
  "Top-3 concentration: high single-name risk. Held 62 distinct names over the backtest, rotating ~3 at a time.",
  "Frictionless backtest: ignores ~210%/yr turnover cost, slippage, and short-term-gains tax. Net returns will be lower.",
  "Current holdings = live position as of 2026-06-16; next rebalance projected 2026-11-10 (105-day hold)."
 ]
